        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "language": "html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    \n  </head>\n  <body>\n    \n    <!-- Page Title -->\n    <h1>Willow Grove Animal Shelter</h1>\n    \n    <!-- Shelter information -->\n    <p>At Willow Grove Animal Shelter, we are dedicated to rescuing, rehabilitating, and rehoming animals in need. Our mission is to provide a safe haven for homeless pets and to work tirelessly towards a world where every animal is loved and cared for. Through community engagement, education, and compassion, we strive to create lasting bonds between people and pets.</p>\n    \n  \n    <hr>\n    \n    <!-- Animals up for adoption with name and bulleted list of their information -->\n    <h2>Adoption Showcase</h2>\n    \n    <h3>Bella</h3>\n    \n    <ul>\n      <li>Age: 2 years</li>\n      <li>Breed: Labrador Retriever</li>\n      <li>Personality: Engergetic, friendly, great with kids</li>\n    </ul>\n    \n    \n    <h3>Smoke</h3>\n\n    <ul>\n      <li>Age: 3 years</li>\n      <li>Breed: Russian Blue</li>\n      <li>Personality: Independent, intelligent, loves sunbathing</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    \n    <h3>Max</h3>\n\n    <ul>\n      <li>Age: 5 years</li>\n      <li>Breed: German Shepherd</li>\n      <li>Personality: Loyal, protective, enjoys long walks</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    \n    <h3>Daisy</h3>\n\n    <ul>\n      <li>Age: 6 months</li>\n      <li>Breed: Mixed Breed</li>\n      <li>Personality: Playful, curious, good with other pets</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    \n    <h3>Puck</h3>\n\n    <ul>\n      <li>Age: 4 years</li>\n      <li>Breed: Tuxedo Cat</li>\n      <li>Personality: Calm, affectionate, loves attention</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    \n    <h3>Rocky</h3>\n\n    <ul>\n      <li>Age: 1 year</li>\n      <li>Breed: Beagle</li>\n      <li>Personality: Adventurous, friendly, great sense of smell</li>\n    </ul>\n\n  \n    <hr>\n    \n    <!-- Volunteer Information Section -->\n    <h2>Volunteer Information</h2>\n    \n    <h3>Introduction to Volunteering</h3>\n    \n    <p>Join our dedicated team of volunteers at Willow Grove Animal Shelter and make a difference in the lives of animals. Whether you have a few hours a week or can commit more time, your help is invaluable.</p>\n    \n    <!-- Numbered list of roles available at the shelter for volunteers, bulleted list within numbered list of role responsibilities  -->\n    <h3>Roles and Responsibilities</h3>\n    \n    <ol>\n      <li>Animal Care</li>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Feeding</li>\n          <li>Grooming</li>\n          <li>Exercising pets</li>\n        </ul>\n      <br>\n      <li>Event Assistance</li>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Helping with fundraising events and adoption drives</li>\n        </ul>\n      <br>\n      <li>Shelter Maintenance</li>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Assisting with cleaning and upkeep of the shelter</li>\n        </ul>\n    </ol>\n    \n    <h3>Time Commitment</h3>\n    \n    <p>Flexible schedules available, ranging from a few hours per week to full-time volunteer work.</p>\n    \n    <h3>Contact for Interest</h3>\n    \n    <p>Email: volunteer@willowgroveshelter.org <br>\n      Phone: (555) 123-4567 ext. 2</p>\n    \n    <hr>\n    \n    <!-- Bulleted list of educational information within bulleted list of topic -->\n    <h2>Educational Resources</h2>\n    \n    <h3>Pet Nutrition Guide</h3>\n    \n    <ul>\n      <li>Balanced Diet:</li>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Dogs: High-quality dog food with a balance of protein, carbohydrates, fats, vitamins, and minerals.</li>\n          <li>Cats: Nutrient-rich cat food, high in protein with moderate fat levels, and low carbohydrates.</li>\n        </ul>\n      <br>\n      <li>Feeding Schedule:</li>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Puppies/Kittens: Feed 3-4 times a day.</li>\n          <li>Adult Dogs/Cats: Feed 1-2 times a day.</li>\n        </ul>\n      <br>\n      <li>Special Diets:</li>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Consult a veterinarian for pets with specific dietary needs such as allergies, obesity, or health conditions.</li>\n        </ul>\n      <br>\n      <li>Hydration:</li>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Ensure fresh water is available at all times.</li>\n        </ul>\n    </ul>\n    \n    <h3>Training Information</h3>\n    \n    <ul>\n      <li>Basic Commands:</li>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Teach basic commands like sit, stay, come, and heel through positive reinforcement.</li>\n        </ul>\n      <br>\n      <li>Socialization:</li>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Expose pets to different people, animals, and environments to develop well-adjusted behavior.</li>\n        </ul>\n      <br>\n      <li>Behavioral Training:</li>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Address issues like excessive barking, chewing, or scratching through consistent training and professional advice if needed.</li>\n        </ul>\n      <br>\n      <li>Training Resources:</li>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Recommend professional trainers or training classes for more in-depth guidance</li>\n        </ul>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h3>Grooming Information</h3>\n    \n    <ul>\n      <li>Coat Care:</li>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Dogs: Regular brushing, depending on the breed. Bathing as needed.</li>\n          <li>Cats: Regular brushing to reduce hairballs, especially for long-haired breeds.</li>\n        </ul>\n      <br>\n      <li>Nail Trimming:</li>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Regular nail trims to prevent discomfort and health issues.</li>\n        </ul>\n      <br>\n      <li>Ear and Teeth Cleaning:</li>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Clean ears to prevent infections and brush teeth to promote dental health.</li>\n        </ul>\n      <br>\n      <li>Professional Grooming:</li>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Some pets may require professional grooming, especially those with longer coats</li>\n        </ul>\n    </ul>\n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n    \n\n      \n\n    \n  </body>\n</html>",
          "active": false,
